{"seq":13,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-08-saltmarsh-summary/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:41:54.390Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"f5783d92267d0cdbf88a2f606f6cb24e4494d6a876dcd7e353858494d794091a","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Sofia, here's what I found for the Saltmarsh Provisions summary:\n\n1. Handover: Bettina Kroll took it over from you on Monday 6 Oct 2025. Moss's Coastal Sunday prep (5 Oct 2025) says the account \"changes hands tomorrow, Monday, October 6\". It doesn't name the new owner. The channel does: on 15 Oct you call it \"Bettina's grocery account\", and on 17 Nov Bettina calls it \"Sofia's old grocery account\". I took the date from Moss's note and the name from those messages. Don't confuse this with the Pellucid Harbor Logistics handoff (3 Nov, then Kwame on 22 Nov). That is a different account.\n\n2. Discount: 10%. On 17 Nov 2025 Bettina first posted 12%, then corrected it within minutes: \"please ignore my earlier note, it's 10%\". She had misread June Osei-Lark's draft worksheet. That correction is the only confirmation I can see. I haven't seen the finalised paperwork, so check it against June's worksheet if the file needs to be exact.\n\n3. Corinne's admin access issue: ticket PD-4827. Kwame opened it on 15 Oct 2025 after her Pemberline Dock admin rights disappeared. Don't use PD-4824. That is a separate ticket, about the refrigerated loads moved from door 3 to door 4 in the exception report.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
